          "question": "If a note says \"use additional code\", is that optional?",
          "answer": "Not medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.\n\nThe search results don't answer this directly. They don't say whether \"use additional code\" is always required or sometimes optional.\n\nThe coding conventions summary (ICD-10-CM code structure and the conventions that govern selection) says \"code first\" and \"use additional code\" appear as a pair and fix the order of reporting. An underlying condition is reported before its manifestation. It does not say whether the second code can be skipped.\n\nThe diabetes summary (Coding type 2 diabetes: E11) and the heart failure summary (Coding heart failure: I50) both describe cases where the additional code is added to a main code, so it carries detail the main code lacks. Neither says it is always mandatory.\n\nFor a definite answer, check the official ICD-10-CM Official Guidelines for Coding and Reporting, or ask a certified medical coder. Coding rules can change between years.",
